    "name":  "Epididymo-orchitis",
    "module":  "male-genital",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Epididymo-orchitis is inflammation of the epididymis (epididymitis) and testis (orchitis), most commonly due to bacterial infection spreading from the urethra or bladder. In sexually active men under 35, Chlamydia trachomatis and Neisseria gonorrhoeae are the most common causes. In older men and boys, enteric organisms (E. coli, Klebsiella) predominate, often associated with urinary tract pathology. It presents with gradual-onset scrotal pain, swelling, warmth, and erythema, typically accompanied by fever, dysuria, and urethral discharge. Treatment is with appropriate antibiotics; empirical therapy covers both STI and enteric organisms until cultures confirm the cause.",
